// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
//
// `i32 x = -2147483648;` -- the positive magnitude 2147483648
// (2^31) does not fit i32's positive range, but its negation is
// exactly i32's minimum, a perfectly legal value. Was rejected
// diag.literal-out-of-range (static) by the checker (no
// expected-type threading, and no negated-value range check) and
// again when it ran (the positive magnitude was evaluated
// with no expected type before negating).

import std;
fn main()
{
    if (!({ i32 x = -2147483648; x == -2147483648 }))
    {
        1 /(1 - 1);
    }
}
